## Environment constraint honored

The only test tier in this project is Vitest inside workerd
(`@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers`; see `docs/context/testing.md`). There is
no DOM/browser/e2e tier. `docs/context/methodology.md`'s "Scope of the
practice" section states explicitly that test-first here does not mean React
component tests, and that a purely visual acceptance criterion produces no
test file. Both in-scope PRD ACs (AC-1, AC-5) mix a pure-logic, testable slice
(what `parseShareTarget` returns) with a DOM-rendered, gesture-based slice
(pre-fill, autofocus, save confirmation, actual POST from the UI) that is
structurally unreachable from workerd. This suite writes real, discriminative
tests for the testable slice and documents the untestable slice's manual
verification path below rather than inventing a component test or asserting
nothing.

