### Per-AC note: what is and is not covered by the new test file

**AC-1 share-creates-task.** The plan splits this PRD AC across AC-A1, AC-A2,
AC-A4, AC-A5 (see plan `## Acceptance Criteria`). Of these:
- AC-A1's `parseShareTarget` extraction, and AC-A5's Android url-often-empty
  quirk (text still wins), are covered by real, discriminative Vitest cases
  above.
- AC-A1's remaining slice — the capture field opening pre-filled, the Save
  action, and the confirmation message appearing — is DOM/React-rendered
  (`src/app/App.tsx`) and unreachable from the workerd-only Vitest tier. It is
  verified manually per the plan's Level 3 MANUAL step 1 ("Share non-empty
  text from another installed app... confirm the capture field opens
  pre-filled... a Task is created... and a confirmation message appears").
  This is the `EXISTING_COVERAGE_SUFFICIENT`-adjacent, no-test-required path
  `docs/context/methodology.md`'s "Scope of the practice" section names for
  purely visual/gesture behavior — not a coverage gap this session left
  silently unaddressed.
- AC-A2 (the `share_target` manifest member's shape) is a static JSON
  invariant on a non-code asset, not application logic; the plan's own Level 2
  Validation Commands verify it with a `node -e` script, not Vitest. No test
  file is authored for it here — writing one would duplicate that existing,
  plan-specified validation path.
- AC-A4 (the created payload must be a `CreateTaskInput` sent through the
  existing `createTask()` wrapper, never a hand-written `TaskDto`-shaped
  literal) is a structural/authorship invariant indistinguishable from the
  wire format at the HTTP boundary — a conforming payload and a hand-written
  literal that happens to match the same shape produce an identical, not
  discriminable, POST body. This is `code-reviewer`'s R-X hand-duplicated-type
  check, not a runtime-observable contract a unit test can discriminate.

**AC-5 empty-share-creates-nothing.** The plan's AC-A3 is the sole PRD AC-5
reference. Covered:
- `parseShareTarget` returning `null` for the all-empty and
  all-whitespace-only cases (3 discriminative cases above).
- Not covered by a new test: the capture field opening focused-and-empty, and
  no Task being created, when `initialShare` is `null`. This is DOM/React
  rendering plus the pre-existing, unmodified
  `if (!trimmed || busy) return` guard in `src/app/App.tsx` (plan line 118) —
  neither is reachable from workerd. Verified manually per the plan's Level 3
  MANUAL step 2. The guard itself is pre-existing and already exercised
  indirectly by `test/tasks.test.ts`'s "rejects invalid input" case
  (`title: "   "` → 400) at the API boundary; this phase adds no new guard
  logic to re-test.

